{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"web_search","id":"exec-56975fda-50ca-4171-a007-05bcdc8a5c77","query":"site:modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/basic/transports streamable HTTP Accept application/json text/event-stream session GET DELETE origin ...","action":{"type":"search","queries":["site:modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/basic/transports streamable HTTP Accept application/json text/event-stream session GET DELETE origin","site:modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/basic/lifecycle protocol version negotiation initialize unsupported version","site:modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools structuredContent outputSchema tool execution error"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"php.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"A tool that wants to branch on the revision itself can read it from the injected `RequestContext`, see Talking back to the client. ... The","title":"Tools - MCP PHP SDK","url":"https://php.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/servers/tools/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"ruby.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"This means top-level values are bound through keyword arguments (`def call(message:, payload: nil, server_context:)`), and nested objects must be read with symbol keys: ... >","title":"Tools | MCP Ruby SDK","url":"https://ruby.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/server/tools/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"java.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"During `initialize()`, the client sends the list of protocol versions its transport supports (newest first) and the server picks one it also supports. ... Built-in","title":"MCP Client - MCP Java SDK","url":"https://java.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/latest-snapshot/client/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"ruby.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"Per the SEP-2575 era model, an era is a property of the protocol version itself: ... `configuration = MCP::Configuration.new(protocol_version: \"2025-06-18\") ... ## Client Negotiation`MCP::Client#conne","title":"Protocol Versions | MCP Ruby SDK","url":"https://ruby.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/protocol-versions/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"`structured_content` is the tool's return value as JSON, matching the tool's declared `output_schema`. ... The `ToolError`'s message landed in `content`, where the model can read","title":"The Client - MCP Python SDK","url":"https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/client/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"ts.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"\"message\": \"Unsupported protocol version: 2025-06-18\", ... Behind an Express body parser the Node stream is already drained: build the `Request` the predicate takes with `toWebRequest(req,","title":"Support legacy clients | MCP TypeScript SDK","url":"https://ts.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/v2/serving/legacy-clients"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"go.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"The MCP specification defines two lifecycle models, and the SDK supports both transparently based on the negotiated protocol version: ... * A stateless model introduced","title":"LifeCycle - MCP Go SDK","url":"https://go.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/protocol/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"php.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"This follows the protocol version negotiation section of the specification. ... ProtocolVersion::V2025_11_25->isAtLeast(ProtocolVersion::V2025_06_18); // true ... * `logging/setLevel` — replaced by `_","title":"Protocol versions - MCP PHP SDK","url":"https://php.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/protocol-versions/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"go.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"* Marshal the tool's structured output (if any) to JSON, and store it in the result's `StructuredContent` field as well as the unstructured `Content` field.","title":"MCP Server - MCP Go SDK","url":"https://go.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/server/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"Raise `MCPError` and the protocol sees it. ... `ToolError`, from `mcp.server.mcpserver.exceptions`, is how a tool tells the model that something went wrong. ... * `is_error`","title":"Handling errors - MCP Python SDK","url":"https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/servers/handling-errors/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"\"2025-06-18\", ... Protocol revisions reachable via the initialize handshake. ... ## LATEST_PROTOCOL_VERSION `module-attribute`","title":"version - MCP Python SDK","url":"https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/api/mcp_types/version/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"logger.warning(f\"Tool {name} not listed by server, cannot validate any structured content\") ... raise RuntimeError(f\"Tool {name} has an output schema but did not return structured content\")","title":"client - MCP Python SDK","url":"https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/api/mcp/client/"}]}}
